    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303-a4">

                <pb facs="0365" n="1099" xml:id="pg1099"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 151.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Breckinridge to Mr.
                            Rawicz.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your No. 1528. M. C., of
                    the 24th instant, stating that you have made inquiry about Anton Yablkowski, a
                    citizen of the United States, detained in the city of Nieszawa, referred to in
                    your letter of September 11, and that you will report the result of your
                    inquiries as soon as ascertained. I address an inquiry to the foreign office and
                    also await your further advices as indicated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifton R. Breckinridge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
